WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:06.629
You know, for all of the fear mongering about
Democrats really being socialists, Obama was

00:00:06.629 --> 00:00:07.649
a Marxist.

00:00:07.649 --> 00:00:09.110
Bernie is a communist.

00:00:09.110 --> 00:00:12.030
All of this stuff, you've been seeing it for
years.

00:00:12.030 --> 00:00:18.331
Is it possible that Donald Trump is the most
socialist president that we've ever had, or

00:00:18.331 --> 00:00:20.369
at least in decades?

00:00:20.369 --> 00:00:25.619
You know, we did a story a year or two ago
about is Donald Trump the first atheist president?

00:00:25.619 --> 00:00:30.810
We talked about other non-religious presidents
or presidents believed to be non-religious.

00:00:30.810 --> 00:00:35.320
And we talked about the reality that Donald
Trump appears to be lying about being religious

00:00:35.320 --> 00:00:39.460
just to try to play, Kate, evangelical voters.

00:00:39.460 --> 00:00:44.280
It doesn't make Trump a better president not
to be religious, but he just might not be

00:00:44.280 --> 00:00:48.260
religious despite his claims that he loves
the Bible and all of this stuff.

00:00:48.260 --> 00:00:49.500
Well, what about Trump?

00:00:49.500 --> 00:00:54.740
As a socialist president now, to be clear,
Trump is not a socialist, but we are talking

00:00:54.740 --> 00:01:01.020
here about the sort of haphazard definition
of socialism and communism that the right

00:01:01.020 --> 00:01:05.630
likes to wrongly ascribe to the ideas of the
left.

00:01:05.630 --> 00:01:11.290
But there is a long list of the socialization
of some elements of the economy by Donald

00:01:11.290 --> 00:01:18.780
Trump that could arguably make Trump the closest
thing we've had to the definition of a socialist

00:01:18.780 --> 00:01:24.630
president that his supporters tend to ascribe
to socialism.

00:01:24.630 --> 00:01:29.470
Now, you know, to be clear, there's socialism
and then there's sort of like social democracy

00:01:29.470 --> 00:01:31.790
that is sometimes called socialism.

00:01:31.790 --> 00:01:33.180
I understand that.

00:01:33.180 --> 00:01:38.610
But let's consider this and use the spectrum,
because that's really what it is in terms

00:01:38.610 --> 00:01:43.720
of government stimulus, which the right loves
to call socialism.

00:01:43.720 --> 00:01:49.550
The first corona virus relief package was
two point two trillion in the Keres Act, trillions

00:01:49.550 --> 00:01:54.300
coming in additional forms, trillions pumped
into the market by the Fed.

00:01:54.300 --> 00:01:59.460
This is way, way, way bigger than the Obama
stimulus, which they called socialist.

00:01:59.460 --> 00:02:05.980
Remember, Obama was a socialist for an 800
billion dollar stimulus bill and for mandating

00:02:05.980 --> 00:02:11.009
you buy private health insurance from for
profit companies.

00:02:11.009 --> 00:02:15.209
Bush's bank bailout was about 400 billion.

00:02:15.209 --> 00:02:18.310
This is like eight trillion in total.

00:02:18.310 --> 00:02:24.270
Trump used the Defense Production Act to force
General Motors to make ventilator's after

00:02:24.270 --> 00:02:26.990
initial talks broke down over costs.

00:02:26.990 --> 00:02:31.840
This is heavy government involvement in directing
the activities of private industry, something

00:02:31.840 --> 00:02:36.990
that the right loves to call socialism in
Soviet Russia.

00:02:36.990 --> 00:02:40.640
The government tells you what kind of bread
to make.

00:02:40.640 --> 00:02:44.319
Trump threatened to condition the sale tick.

00:02:44.319 --> 00:02:51.770
Talk to Microsoft on the U.S. receiving a
very big portion of the sale price and said

00:02:51.770 --> 00:02:57.540
that nobody else thinks about deals this way
other than him straight up saying government

00:02:57.540 --> 00:02:59.860
will take a cut.

00:02:59.860 --> 00:03:02.700
Of a private business deal, because why?

00:03:02.700 --> 00:03:04.239
Because Trump wants a cut.

00:03:04.239 --> 00:03:08.720
If Barack Obama had ever suggested anything
like this, Fox News would have gone bananas

00:03:08.720 --> 00:03:09.910
for 10 days.

00:03:09.910 --> 00:03:16.700
Donald Trump has massively expanded direct
farm aid from 11 billion in 2017 to more than

00:03:16.700 --> 00:03:19.030
thirty two billion in 2020.

00:03:19.030 --> 00:03:23.640
Also, he could pay off the farmers who were
hurt by his trade war.

00:03:23.640 --> 00:03:30.540
He has socialized a larger portion of agriculture
than previous presidents.

00:03:30.540 --> 00:03:35.629
When Harley Davidson wanted to move some of
its manufacturing over to Europe, Trump threatened

00:03:35.629 --> 00:03:39.989
them with regulating them and taxing them
like never before.

00:03:39.989 --> 00:03:45.510
This is extraordinarily heavy handed in terms
of a government crackdown on a business that

00:03:45.510 --> 00:03:50.860
the right calls socialist when a Democrat
suggests doing it.

00:03:50.860 --> 00:03:58.180
Trump moved to prop up the local the domestic
coal industry, despite the market deciding

00:03:58.180 --> 00:03:59.670
it's time to wrap up coal.

00:03:59.670 --> 00:04:00.900
Coal doesn't make sense.

00:04:00.900 --> 00:04:07.180
The government is overriding markets to decide
which industry will succeed or fail.

00:04:07.180 --> 00:04:08.180
Wow.

00:04:08.180 --> 00:04:10.129
And whereas the right on this.

00:04:10.129 --> 00:04:12.879
Trump has also raised the deficit massively.

00:04:12.879 --> 00:04:19.579
Obama left office with about a 500 billion
deficit, down from one point five trillion.

00:04:19.579 --> 00:04:22.250
Remember that deficit, not debt.

00:04:22.250 --> 00:04:27.009
Trump doubled where Barack Obama left off
before Corona virus.

00:04:27.009 --> 00:04:31.159
And now, obviously with coronavirus, everything
is completely out of control.

00:04:31.159 --> 00:04:36.009
The right loves to say those socialist Democrats
raise the deficit.

00:04:36.009 --> 00:04:37.900
But it's Trump who's done it historically.

00:04:37.900 --> 00:04:42.039
Trump, when asked about debt and deficit,
deflects and talks about, you know, we've

00:04:42.039 --> 00:04:47.720
got to build up the military and the wall
and that's going to help the overall economy,

00:04:47.720 --> 00:04:53.939
which is almost like a modern monetary theory
type argument, which is just do the projects

00:04:53.939 --> 00:04:55.599
and the economy will benefit.

00:04:55.599 --> 00:04:57.729
Except Trump's doing it with the wrong projects.

00:04:57.729 --> 00:05:01.879
That would make sense to say, you know, improving
health care and education in the short run

00:05:01.879 --> 00:05:03.610
might increase the deficit.

00:05:03.610 --> 00:05:08.099
But we will benefit so much that in the long
run, it will actually be deficit negative

00:05:08.099 --> 00:05:09.099
or deficit neutral.

00:05:09.099 --> 00:05:11.910
Trump sort of making that argument.

00:05:11.910 --> 00:05:14.770
But with the wrong things like building a
wall as an example.

00:05:14.770 --> 00:05:20.249
Now, Trump supporters will say Trump didn't
want to do any socialism, but he had to do

00:05:20.249 --> 00:05:23.110
it because of corona virus for the good of
the country.

00:05:23.110 --> 00:05:25.509
And that's true, too, to a certain degree.

00:05:25.509 --> 00:05:27.699
But it's what he did nonetheless.

00:05:27.699 --> 00:05:30.979
A true capitalist would have said, let the
businesses fail.

00:05:30.979 --> 00:05:35.099
If you don't want to fly because of a virus,
let the airlines go under.

00:05:35.099 --> 00:05:37.819
That's not what Donald Trump is doing.

00:05:37.819 --> 00:05:41.180
It's also the experience of FDR, by the way.

00:05:41.180 --> 00:05:49.129
I mean, he arguably somewhat reluctantly came
to some of the policies he came to in order

00:05:49.129 --> 00:05:51.900
to kind of save capitalism from itself.

00:05:51.900 --> 00:05:58.129
Now, FDR is seen by some as the most socialist
president we've had.

00:05:58.129 --> 00:06:00.999
Trump has arguably done more.

00:06:00.999 --> 00:06:04.689
Presidents have to respond to the events of
their presidency, that's for sure.

00:06:04.689 --> 00:06:07.099
You can't remove corona virus from it.

00:06:07.099 --> 00:06:13.460
Sort of like imagining Lincoln's presidency
without the civil war or FDR presidency, without

00:06:13.460 --> 00:06:16.689
recovering from the Great Depression and World
War Two.

00:06:16.689 --> 00:06:19.809
Trump had to deal with Corona virus, but he
chose to do it this way.

00:06:19.809 --> 00:06:21.500
It could have been done other ways.

00:06:21.500 --> 00:06:26.180
Now, of course, Trump has also done other
things that are not socialistic, right?

00:06:26.180 --> 00:06:31.530
He's deregulated business so business can
pollute more, so cars can be less efficient.

00:06:31.530 --> 00:06:34.810
Cut funding to agencies, cut taxes for some
people.

00:06:34.810 --> 00:06:39.740
But despite all of that, by many measures,
Trump could still be the most socialistic

00:06:39.740 --> 00:06:42.490
president in many of our lifetimes.

00:06:42.490 --> 00:06:46.430
You've got to go back at least to Nixon, who
created the EPA.

00:06:46.430 --> 00:06:50.679
OSHA boosted regulations, Social Security
benefits.

00:06:50.679 --> 00:06:55.370
Maybe you'd go back to Dwight Eisenhower,
who passed the Interstate Highway Act.

00:06:55.370 --> 00:07:01.240
Subsidized mortgages and college tuition had
a 91 percent top marginal tax rate, despite

00:07:01.240 --> 00:07:04.490
lots of ways to reduce the effective tax rate.

00:07:04.490 --> 00:07:06.529
What's the reaction from Trump pests?

00:07:06.529 --> 00:07:08.339
Absolutely none.

00:07:08.339 --> 00:07:12.680
They're too busy trying to suppress the vote
to actually care about what it is that Donald

00:07:12.680 --> 00:07:13.789
Trump is doing.

00:07:13.789 --> 00:07:14.789
Weird times.

00:07:14.789 --> 00:07:14.794
We live in my friends.

